# CR 704.5q: "If a permanent has both a +1/+1 counter and a -1/-1 counter on it, N +1/+1 and N -1/-1 counters are removed
# from it, where N is the smaller of the number of +1/+1 and -1/-1 counters on it." Bot1's Ornithopter gets a +1/+1 counter
# from Innkeeper's Talent's combat trigger on turn 1. On turn 3 Bot1 blights 1 as it casts Requiting Hex (CR 701.68a),
# putting a -1/-1 counter on the Ornithopter; before Bot1 next has priority the two counters are removed, so it has none and
# is a 0/2 again. The Hex then destroys Bot2's Ornithopter and Bot1 gains 2 life.

